## Testing Interface Implementations

### The Interface Under Test

```xiom
interface Validator {
  fn validate(&self, input: Str) -> Bool;
  fn error_message(&self) -> Str;
}
```

### Test Strategy

Test each implementation for:
1. **Valid inputs** — should return true
2. **Invalid inputs** — should return false
3. **Edge cases** — empty string, max length, boundary values
4. **Error messages** — should be descriptive and not empty

### Testing Email Validator

```xiom
fn test_email_validator() -> Bool {
  let v = EmailValidator{};

  assert(v.validate("user@example.com") == true);
  assert(v.validate("a@b.co") == true);
  assert(v.validate("notanemail") == false);
  assert(v.validate("@") == false);
  assert(v.validate("") == false);
  assert(v.error_message().len() > 0);

  true
}
```

### Testing All Implementations at Once

```xiom
fn run_all_tests() {
  assert(test_email_validator());
  assert(test_password_validator());
  assert(test_age_validator());
  io.println("All interface tests passed!");
}
```

